evidence.en:
useEffect(() => {
  const ws = connect('/feed');
  ws.on('msg', append);
}, []);   // no return statement

dev log:  connect /feed
dev log:  connect /feed     <- second live socket

StrictMode in dev runs every mount as setup, ___b1___, setup; because this effect never returns a ___b2___, the first socket is never closed and two stay alive. The effect was already wrong: in production the same double-connect appears on any route ___b3___, so the fix is closing the socket in the effect, not removing StrictMode.

